Subject: [PATCH] mtd: rawnand: add full-ID entries for 2 Gbit parallel NANDs

Required on the FiberHome HG5382A: its Winbond W29N02KVSIAF is not ONFI
(onfi_ver=0), and without a full-ID entry its extended ID decodes to a
64-byte OOB instead of 128.  Full-ID entries fix the OOB size of common
2 Gbit SLC parts whose extended-ID decode is ambiguous (64 vs 128 byte
OOB).  The EN7581 PNAND driver derives its BCH strength from
mtd->oobsize, so a wrong OOB size means a page layout that nothing else
in the boot chain reads back.  Linux carries the W29N02KV entries
(target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/904); the others are U-Boot and BL2
only, so a board on one of them needs its Linux entry added too.

The W29N02KVSIAF is listed at ECC4, what the part asks for and what
pbs05/uboot-an758x runs it at in BL2 and U-Boot (spare 28): the driver
picks the lowest strength at or above the declared one.  BL2
(arm-trusted-firmware-airoha patches/100) and Linux (patches-6.18/903 and
904) use the same codeword: ECC4, data inverted, all 8 FDM bytes covered,
so what one writes the others read, and the UBI pbs05's U-Boot wrote
attaches as it is.

The stock FiberHome firmware writes ECC8 with another codeword; its UBI
fails every page with -74, and a board coming from stock has its UBI
rebuilt the first time it runs this U-Boot.

Taken from https://github.com/pbs05/uboot-an758x (manufacturer ops files
and the NAND_MFR_* additions are not carried).

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/nand_ids.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/nand_ids.c
@@ -32,6 +32,46 @@
 		{ .id = {0x98, 0xd1, 0x90, 0x15, 0x76, 0x14, 0x01, 0x00} },
 		  SZ_2K, SZ_128, SZ_128K, 0, 8, 64, NAND_ECC_INFO(1, SZ_512),
 		  2 },
+	{"TC58NVG1S3HTAI0 2G 3.3V 8-bit",
+		{ .id = {0x98, 0xda, 0x90, 0x15, 0x76} },
+		  SZ_2K, SZ_256, SZ_128K, 0, 5, 128,
+		  NAND_ECC_INFO(8, SZ_512), 0 },
+	{"W29N02GV 2G 3.3V 8-bit",
+		{ .id = {0xef, 0xda, 0x90, 0x95, 0x04} },
+		  SZ_2K, SZ_256, SZ_128K, 0, 5, 64,
+		  NAND_ECC_INFO(1, SZ_512), 0 },
+	{"W29N02KVSIAE 2G 3.3V 8-bit",
+		{ .id = {0xef, 0xda, 0x10, 0x95, 0x07} },
+		  SZ_2K, SZ_256, SZ_128K, 0, 5, 128,
+		  NAND_ECC_INFO(8, SZ_512), 0 },
+	{"W29N02KVSIAF 2G 3.3V 8-bit",
+		{ .id = {0xef, 0xda, 0x10, 0x95, 0x06} },
+		  SZ_2K, SZ_256, SZ_128K, 0, 5, 128,
+		  NAND_ECC_INFO(4, SZ_512), 0 },
+	{"S34ML02G300TFI00 2G 3.3V 8-bit",
